":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques","title":"MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/VertexNotFound":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" call throws when a vertex it was given isn’t in the graph."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexNotFound","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexNotFound"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/vertexnotfound","title":"VertexNotFound","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexNotFound"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://Cliques/documentation/Cliques/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/graphprotocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques